# Sections the harness expects to find in this repo's root CLAUDE.md.
#
# One `## ` heading per line, copied from the harness's
# template/CLAUDE-sections.md. `.github/scripts/claude-sections-check.sh`
# fails the build when a listed heading is missing, which is what turns
# "splice these sections in" from a printed instruction into a gate.
#
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Match is on the exact heading
# line, so a repo may reword a section's *body* freely — the heading is the
# contract, the prose under it is the repo's own.
#
# When the harness adds a section, this file changes with it; a consumer
# picks the change up on its next sync and its CI goes red until the section
# is spliced. That is deliberate — the redness IS the notification, since
# nothing else tells a repo the shared guidance has moved.

## Definition of Done
## Code Style
## Commit Workflow
## Worklog
## Architecture decisions (ADRs)
## Schema conventions
## Tenant scoping
## Mistakes
